<p>I often use <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">history</code> to view command history, but there’s already a ready-made shortcut for it.</p>

<p>After pressing <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Ctrl + R</code>, type the keyword to search for; if it’s not the one you want, keep pressing <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Ctrl + R</code> to iterate through the matches.</p>

<p>This command actually queries through the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">history</code> records as well. If you don’t like this approach, you can just do <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">history | grep xxx</code>, which works just as well.</p>

